## Bicubic PatchMesh under a step=1 basis (b-spline), periodic on u at
## nu=3 -- validPeriodicBicubicMeshDim's true safety floor for step=1
## (gmanpatchpolyobjectmanager.cpp), one below the old (unsafe) floor of
## nu=1. Regression guard for the F1 fix: three concentric triangular
## control rings (radius 0.45, 0.35, 0.25, 0.15 across the four
## nonperiodic v rows) wrapping u's last strip back to control point 0,
## proving the tightened bound still accepts and correctly renders every
## periodic mesh a step=1 basis can legally form at its minimum.
##
## A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
## desync convention."
Display "patchmesh_bspline_periodic.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Sides 2
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [0]
Basis "b-spline" 1 "b-spline" 1
AttributeBegin
	Translate -1 0 0
	PatchMesh "bicubic" 3 "periodic" 4 "nonperiodic" "P" [
		 0.45     0.0     0  -0.225    0.3897  0  -0.225   -0.3897  0
		 0.35     0.0     0  -0.175    0.3031  0  -0.175   -0.3031  0
		 0.25     0.0     0  -0.125    0.2165  0  -0.125   -0.2165  0
		 0.15     0.0     0  -0.075    0.1299  0  -0.075   -0.1299  0
	]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
	Translate 1 0 0
	Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
